    "title": "Eastern Shore Theatre announces Fall programs, auditions, and classes - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sinclair Krause ,\n1 hours ago\nVideo above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from July 22, 2026\nDAPHNE, Ala. (WKRG) — Eastern Shore Repertory Theatre launches its fall season with a variety of opportunities for students, educators and community members to get involved in the performing arts.\nTexas family loses SUV to Bertha’s dangerous surf Students in grades 5th through 12th are invited to audition for Disney’s High School Musical JR. on Aug. 10 and 11 at 6 p.m. to 8 p.m. at the Nicholson Center for the Arts.\nThe performance on Thursday, Nov. 5, and Friday, Nov. 6, at 9 a.m. and 11 a.m. at the Daphne Civic Center in celebration of the musical’s 20th anniversary.\nThe production aims to give young performers of all experience levels the chance to develop confidence, teamwork and leadership skills through live theatre.\nEastern Shore Rep is also welcoming school groups from pre-kindergarten through 12th grade to attend special daytime performances of the musical.\nLocal Mexican restaurant suffers from third break-in; cash tips and equipment stolen Student and chaperone tickets are $7, while teachers receive complimentary admission. The field trips are designed to introduce students to live theatre while encouraging creativity, collaboration and self-expression.\nClick here to book a field trip.\nFor younger performers, the organization’s Kids Academy will offer musical theatre classes for students in kindergarten through sixth grade.\nThis fall’s productions include Disney’s 101 Dalmatians KIDS from Aug. 17 to Nov. 16 and Disney’s The Jungle Book KIDS from Aug. 19 to Nov. 18, with each program ending in a performance for family and friends.\n“Whether you join us from the stage, the audience, the classroom, or behind the scenes, we would love to welcome you into the Eastern Shore Rep community this fall. The doors are open. Let’s create something remarkable together.” Founder, Executive Director and Artistic Director, Erin Langley said.\nLocal Mexican restaurant suffers from third break-in; cash tips and equipment stolen Eastern Shore Rep is also seeking sponsors for its 2026-27 season to help support theatre productions, student scholarships, educational performances and arts programming throughout the community.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
